  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 2.3. Increased capacity of the ILO constituents to engage in a forward-looking international labour standards policy</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Amendments to the Labour Code and a new Law on Labour Inspection Services were adopted by Parliament on 29 September 2020, including through tripartite consultations. From mid-2019 until the adoption of the legal reforms, the ILO provided drafting assistance for the development of the amendments to the LC and the Law on Labour Inspection Services, supported the consultation processes with the social partners through specific meetings, as well as meetings of the Working Group of the Tripartite Social Partnership Commission, and provided advisory services during Parliamentary considerations of the legal reforms.</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">2.3.2 Number of member States with tripartite mechanisms enabling constituents to effectively engage in the implementation of international labour standards at the national level, including reporting to the supervisory bodies</narrative>
    </title>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 2.2. Increased capacity of the member States to apply international labour standards</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">CEACR Observation on the Right to Organise and Collective Bargaining Convention, 1949 (No. 98) / Georgia.

Amendments to the Labour Code were adopted by Parliament on 29 September 2020, including amendments improving conformity with C.98.  In this respect, the CEACR noted the adoption of section 7 with satisfaction. From mid-2019 until the adoption of the legal reforms, the ILO provided drafting assistance for the development of the amendments to the Labour Code, including section 7. The Office also  supported the consultation processes with the social partners through specific meetings, and provided advisory services during Parliamentary considerations of the legal reforms.</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">2.2.1. Number of cases of progress in the application of ratified Conventions noted with satisfaction by the supervisory bodies</narrative>
    </title>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
